Vegn a prender or da la stasis criogena mia avia da pasta madre e ma metter a pachetar puspe.```   *Stasis is a term used in science fiction, but in this context, it refers to a state of suspended animation or preservation. In Romansh, there isn't a direct equivalent, so I've translated it as "stasis criogena" which means "cryogenic stasis" or "cryogenic preservation".   However, if you want a more literal translation without the sci-fi connotation, you could say:   ```Vegn a prender or da la conservaziun mia avia da pasta madre e ma metter a pachetar puspe.```   This translates to "I'll get my sourdough starter out of preservation and start baking again."
